  "question": "Before replacing a legacy context configuration, I need an exact comparison of the state visible to logging. Consider three independent synchronous runs, each using `structlog.BoundLogger` around a fresh `ReturnLogger`, with caching disabled and no processors except those specified below. Begin each run with clean storage.\n\nFor the `contextvars` run, bind ambient `account=\"ambient\", region=\"west\"`, use an ordinary dict logger context and `[merge_contextvars]`, and assemble `base` with bound `account=\"bound\", user=\"u0\"`. Enter `bound_contextvars(account=\"scope\", request=\"r1\")`. Inside it, create `derived = base.bind(user=\"u1\")`, log `derived.info(\"during\", account=\"call\")`, and then bind ambient `region=\"east\", extra=\"kept\"`. Leave the scope and log `base.info(\"after\")`.\n\nFor the `threadlocal` run, perform the same operations using `bind_threadlocal`, `merge_threadlocal`, and `bound_threadlocal`, still with an ordinary dict logger context.\n\nFor the `wrapped_dict` run, use a newly created `wrap_dict(dict)` context class and an empty processor chain. Assemble `base` with `account=\"bound\", region=\"west\", user=\"u0\"`. Enter `tmp_bind(base, account=\"scope\", request=\"r1\")` and call its yielded logger `scoped`. Inside it, create `derived = scoped.bind(user=\"u1\")`, log `derived.info(\"during\", account=\"call\")`, and then call `scoped.bind(region=\"east\", extra=\"kept\")`, discarding that call's return value. Leave the scope and log `base.info(\"after\")`.\n\nReturn a JSON object keyed by `contextvars`, `threadlocal`, and `wrapped_dict`. Each value must contain `during` and `after`, holding the keyword dictionaries delivered to ReturnLogger by those two logging calls, and `base_context` and `derived_context`, holding plain dictionary snapshots of those loggers' contexts after the scope has exited. Ignore deprecation warnings.",
